  "details": "Now, don't get me wrong, I 99.9% of the time am in VR mode (Valve Index + 3 Vive 3.0s BTW), but for that 0.01% of the time that I'm in desktop, there's one thing on my mind;\n\n\"Even 100% mouse sensitivity is too slow, I want raw input.'\n\nThat's why I propose RAW INPUT! As in, using the sensitivity set by the operating system over the setting set by the game.\n\nThis would just be a simple button directly below the mouse sensitivity slider, that says \"Raw Input\". Turn it on, and it starts using the mouse sensitivity you set on the operating system level - for those that prefer to barely nudge the mouse to turn around.",
